{"name":"Czarina","hex":"#775859","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"czarina","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of tsarina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/czarina"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tsarina","blocks":[{"text":"Tsarina is the title of a female autocratic ruler (monarch) of Bulgaria, Serbia, and Russia, or the title of a tsar's wife. The English spelling is derived from the German czarin or zarin, in the same way as the French tsarine / czarine, and the Spanish and Italian czarina / zarina. A tsar's daughter is a tsarevna."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Marfa_Matveevna_by_Workshop_of_Kremlin_Armoury_%28before_1682%2C_GRM%29.jpg/330px-Marfa_Matveevna_by_Workshop_of_Kremlin_Armoury_%28before_1682%2C_GRM%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsarina","wikidata":"Q2918819"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Vasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg/500px-Vasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Vasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg/1280px-Vasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Vasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg/500px-Vasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the young wives of Ivan the Terrible. Painting by Nikolai Nevrev, 19th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVasilisa_Melentieva.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Alexis_I%27s_bride-show_by_G.Sedov_%281882%2C_GTG%29.jpg/500px-Alexis_I%27s_bride-show_by_G.Sedov_%281882%2C_GTG%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb